><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250702112024+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250702112027+10'00'" name="c4a3b5d4-6fc2-4d77-a1dd-d559dae47f11" page="4" coords="311.803406,733.644165,552.742676,733.644165,311.803406,722.738770,552.742676,722.738770,311.803406,721.642212,552.707214,721.642212,311.803406,710.736755,552.707214,710.736755,311.803406,709.640137,552.741699,709.640137,311.803406,698.734741,552.741699,698.734741,311.803406,697.638184,552.680725,697.638184,311.803406,686.732727,552.680725,686.732727,311.803406,685.636108,552.719788,685.636108,311.803406,674.730713,552.719788,674.730713,311.803406,673.634155,552.742676,673.634155,311.803406,662.728699,552.742676,662.728699,311.803406,661.632080,552.767456,661.632080,311.803406,650.726685,552.767456,650.726685,311.803406,649.630127,384.639160,649.630127,311.803406,638.724670,384.639160,638.724670,236.717255,145.656738,297.642395,145.656738,236.717255,134.751328,297.642395,134.751328,56.692917,133.654724,297.661560,133.654724,56.692917,122.749313,297.661560,122.749313,56.692917,121.652725,297.647644,121.652725,56.692917,110.747314,297.647644,110.747314,56.692902,109.650726,297.633850,109.650726,56.692902,98.745316,297.633850,98.745316,56.684402,97.648727,297.581665,97.648727,56.684402,86.743317,297.581665,86.743317,56.684402,85.646729,297.633850,85.646729,56.684402,74.741318,297.633850,74.741318,56.684402,73.644730,297.646759,73.644730,56.684402,62.739319,297.646759,62.739319,56.684402,61.642731,297.633850,61.642731,56.684402,50.737320,297.633850,50.737320" rect="56.343597,50.396515,553.108276,733.984985" subject="Comment on Text" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-11.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>he available evidence&#xD;(though limited in some areas) suggests that cricket can be&#xD;a source of PA, provide a range of health benefits and can enhance&#xD;QOL. Specific risks associated with cricket include injury, particularly&#xD;to the spine, which is most prevalent in bowlers. There was&#xD;consistent evidence to support a positive relationship between increased&#xD;workload and injury risk in bowlers. One in two former&#xD;cricketers reported persistent pain and one in three reported osteoarthritis.&#xD;Cricketers should be informed of the potential long&#xD;term musculoskeletal implications of cricket participation. While&#xD;there was a paucity of general health literature, as many as 38 % of&#xD;retired cricketers may develop skin cancer within Caucasian cricket&#xD;populations. Heat injuries are also a concern, with cricketers having&#xD;the second highest number of heat injuries of all Australian&#xD;sports. Current and retired cricketers reported higher QOL than the&#xD;general population.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="4" rect="595.276001,641.644165,779.276001,733.644165"
/></highlight
